-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1: Subchapter VI (stock transfers), sections 201 and 202.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. The seat layer is dg3-seat.l4.
--
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt of the Delaware Code Online (through 85 Del. Laws, c. 550),
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. `-- src:N | ...` is a slice of line N of that file; an ellipsis means the line goes on.
--
-- Sections 201 and 202 are among those that section 114(c)(3) takes out of the member reading for a nonprofit nonstock corporation;
-- section 202 is not in the list of section 114(b), so the stockholder-to-member reading (section 114(a)) applies to a nonstock corporation with membership interests:
-- this piece does not encode that reading (section 114 is encoded by dg1) and speaks of "securities" and "holders" as the text does.
-- Out of range: Article 8 of subtitle I of Title 6 (not an input), the Internal Revenue Code (26 U.S.C., not an input), section 151(f) (dg3-stock-issue).

§ `Section 201: transfer of stock, stock certificates and uncertificated stock`

-- What governs the transfer of stock.
-- src:614 | Except as otherwise provided in this chapter, the transfer of stock and the certificates of stock which represent the stock or uncertificated stock shall be governed by Article 8 of subtitle I of Title 6. To the extent that any provision of this chapter is inconsistent with any provision of subtitle I of Title 6, this chapter shall be controlling.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 201 (src:614)
DECLARE `s 201 What governs the transfer of stock` IS ONE OF
    `Article 8 of subtitle I of Title 6 under s 201`
    `this chapter under s 201`

-- Except as otherwise provided in the chapter, the transfer of stock and of the certificates that represent it is governed by Article 8 of subtitle I of Title 6;
-- to the extent that any provision of the chapter is inconsistent with a provision of subtitle I of Title 6, the chapter controls.
-- src:614 | To the extent that any provision of this chapter is inconsistent with any provision of subtitle I of Title 6, this chapter shall be controlling.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 201 (src:614)
GIVEN `this chapter otherwise provides for the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision of this chapter is inconsistent with a provision of subtitle I of Title 6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 201 What governs the transfer of stock`
`s 201 what governs the transfer of the stock` `this chapter otherwise provides for the matter` `a provision of this chapter is inconsistent with a provision of subtitle I of Title 6` MEANS
    IF `this chapter otherwise provides for the matter` OR `a provision of this chapter is inconsistent with a provision of subtitle I of Title 6`
    THEN `this chapter under s 201`
    ELSE `Article 8 of subtitle I of Title 6 under s 201`

§ `Section 202: restrictions on transfer and ownership of securities`

-- Section 202(a): a written restriction on the transfer or registration of transfer of a security, or on the amount of the corporation's securities that may be owned by any person or group,
-- if permitted by section 202 and noted conspicuously on the certificate or, for uncertificated shares, contained in the notice given under section 151(f), may be enforced against the holder
-- or any successor or transferee of the holder, including an executor, administrator, trustee, guardian or other fiduciary. Unless so noted, a restriction, even if permitted, is ineffective except against a person with actual knowledge of it.
-- src:618 | A written restriction or restrictions on the transfer or registration of transfer of a security of a corporation, or on the amount of the corporation’s securities that may be owned by any person or group of persons, if permitted by this section and noted conspicuously on the certificate or certificates representing the security or securities so restricted or, in the case of uncertificated shares, contained in the notice or notices given pursuant to § 151(f) of this title, may be enforced against the holder of the restricted security or securities or any successor or transferee of the holder including an executor, administrator, trustee, guardian or other fiduciary entrusted with like responsibility for the person or estate of the holder. Unless noted conspicuously on the certificate or certificates representing the security or securities so restricted or, in the case of uncertificated shares, contained in the notice or notices given pursuant to § 151(f) of this title, a restriction, even though permitted by this section, is ineffective except against a person with actual knowledge of the restriction.
-- src:618 | Unless noted conspicuously on the certificate or certificates representing the security or securities so restricted or, in the case of uncertificated shares, contained in the notice or notices given pursuant to § 151(f) of this title, a restriction, even though permitted by this section, is ineffective except against a person with actual knowledge of the restriction.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 202(a) (src:618)
DECLARE `s 202(a) Facts about a restriction and the person it is asserted against` HAS
    `the restriction is written`                                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the restriction is permitted by section 202`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the restricted securities are represented by a certificate`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the restriction is noted conspicuously on the certificate`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the restriction is contained in the notice given pursuant to section 151(f)`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has actual knowledge of the restriction`                                              IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 202(a) (src:618)
GIVEN f IS A `s 202(a) Facts about a restriction and the person it is asserted against`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 202(a) the restriction may be enforced against the person` f MEANS
        f's `the restriction is written`
    AND f's `the restriction is permitted by section 202`
    AND (    (IF f's `the restricted securities are represented by a certificate`
              THEN f's `the restriction is noted conspicuously on the certificate`
              ELSE f's `the restriction is contained in the notice given pursuant to section 151(f)`)
         OR  f's `the person has actual knowledge of the restriction`)

-- Section 202(b): a restriction may be imposed by the certificate of incorporation, by the bylaws, or by an agreement among any number of security holders or among such holders and the corporation.
-- Any other way is a case the subsection does not address: NOTHING.
-- src:619 | A restriction on the transfer or registration of transfer of securities of a corporation, or on the amount of a corporation’s securities that may be owned by any person or group of persons, may be imposed by the certificate of incorporation or by the bylaws or by an agreement among any number of security holders or among such holders and the corporation. No restrictions so imposed shall be binding with respect to securities issued prior to the adoption of the restriction unless the holders of the securities are parties to an agreement or voted in favor of the restriction.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 202(b) (src:619)
DECLARE `s 202(b) How a restriction is imposed` IS ONE OF
    `by the certificate of incorporation under s 202(b)`
    `by the bylaws under s 202(b)`
    `by an agreement among any number of security holders under s 202(b)`
    `by an agreement among such holders and the corporation under s 202(b)`
    `in another way under s 202(b)`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 202(b) (src:619)
GIVEN how IS A `s 202(b) How a restriction is imposed`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202(b) the restriction may be imposed in that way` how MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `in another way under s 202(b)` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- No restriction so imposed shall be binding with respect to securities issued before the adoption of the restriction unless the holders are parties to an agreement or voted in favor of the restriction.
-- For securities issued after the adoption the sentence says nothing about being binding: NOTHING.
-- src:619 | No restrictions so imposed shall be binding with respect to securities issued prior to the adoption of the restriction unless the holders of the securities are parties to an agreement or voted in favor of the restriction.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 202(b) (src:619)
GIVEN `the securities were issued prior to the adoption of the restriction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holders of the securities are parties to an agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holders of the securities voted in favor of the restriction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202(b) the restriction is binding with respect to the securities` `the securities were issued prior to the adoption of the restriction` `the holders of the securities are parties to an agreement` `the holders of the securities voted in favor of the restriction` MEANS
    IF `the securities were issued prior to the adoption of the restriction`
    THEN JUST (`the holders of the securities are parties to an agreement` OR `the holders of the securities voted in favor of the restriction`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 202(c): a restriction is permitted by section 202 if it (1) obligates the holder to offer the corporation, other holders or any other person a prior opportunity, exercisable within a reasonable time, to acquire the securities;
-- (2) obligates the corporation, a holder or any other person to purchase the securities that are the subject of an agreement respecting their purchase and sale;
-- (3) requires the corporation or the holders of a class or series to consent to a proposed transfer or approve the transferee or the amount that may be owned;
-- (4) obligates the holder to sell or transfer an amount of the securities, or causes their automatic sale or transfer; or
-- (5) prohibits or restricts the transfer to, or the ownership by, designated persons or classes of persons or groups, and the designation is not manifestly unreasonable.
-- Whether the opportunity is exercisable "within a reasonable time", and whether a designation is "manifestly unreasonable", are judgments: inputs.
-- src:620 | A restriction on the transfer or registration of transfer of securities of a corporation or on the amount of such securities that may be owned by any person or group of persons is permitted by this section if it:
-- src:621 | (1) Obligates the holder of the restricted securities to offer to the corporation or to any other holders of securities of the corporation or to any other person or to any combination of the foregoing, a prior opportunity, to be exercised within a reasonable time, to acquire the restricted securities; or
-- src:622 | (2) Obligates the corporation or any holder of securities of the corporation or any other person or any combination of the foregoing, to purchase the securities which are the subject of an agreement respecting the purchase and sale of the restricted securities; or
-- src:623 | (3) Requires the corporation or the holders of any class or series of securities of the corporation to consent to any proposed transfer of the restricted securities or to approve the proposed transferee of the restricted securities, or to approve the amount of securities of the corporation that may be owned by any person or group of persons; or
-- src:624 | (4) Obligates the holder of the restricted securities to sell or transfer an amount of restricted securities to the corporation or to any other holders of securities of the corporation or to any other person or to any combination of the foregoing, or causes or results in the automatic sale or transfer of an amount of restricted securities to the corporation or to any other holders of securities of the corporation or to any other person or to any combination of the foregoing; or
-- src:625 | (5) Prohibits or restricts the transfer of the restricted securities to, or the ownership of restricted securities by, designated persons or classes of persons or groups of persons, and such designation is not manifestly unreasonable.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 202(c) (src:620-625)
DECLARE `s 202(c) The kind of restriction` HAS
    `it obligates the holder to offer to the corporation, other holders or any other person, or any combination, a prior opportunity to acquire the restricted securities` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that opportunity is to be exercised within a reasonable time`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `it obligates the corporation, a holder or any other person, or any combination, to purchase the securities that are the subject of an agreement respecting their purchase and sale` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it requires the corporation or the holders of any class or series to consent to a proposed transfer, to approve the proposed transferee, or to approve the amount of securities that may be owned` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it obligates the holder to sell or transfer an amount of the restricted securities, or causes or results in their automatic sale or transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it prohibits or restricts the transfer to, or the ownership by, designated persons or classes of persons or groups of persons` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the designation is manifestly unreasonable`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 202(c) (src:620-625)
GIVEN k IS A `s 202(c) The kind of restriction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 202(c) the restriction is of a kind that section 202 permits` k MEANS
        (    k's `it obligates the holder to offer to the corporation, other holders or any other person, or any combination, a prior opportunity to acquire the restricted securities`
         AND k's `that opportunity is to be exercised within a reasonable time`)
    OR  k's `it obligates the corporation, a holder or any other person, or any combination, to purchase the securities that are the subject of an agreement respecting their purchase and sale`
    OR  k's `it requires the corporation or the holders of any class or series to consent to a proposed transfer, to approve the proposed transferee, or to approve the amount of securities that may be owned`
    OR  k's `it obligates the holder to sell or transfer an amount of the restricted securities, or causes or results in their automatic sale or transfer`
    OR  (    k's `it prohibits or restricts the transfer to, or the ownership by, designated persons or classes of persons or groups of persons`
         AND (NOT k's `the designation is manifestly unreasonable`))

-- Section 202(d): a restriction for any of the following purposes is conclusively presumed to be for a reasonable purpose: (1) maintaining any local, state, federal or foreign tax advantage to the corporation or its stockholders,
-- including a. status as an electing small business corporation under subchapter S, b. maintaining or preserving any tax attribute (including net operating losses), c. qualifying or maintaining qualification as a real estate investment trust;
-- (2) maintaining any statutory or regulatory advantage or complying with any statutory or regulatory requirements under applicable local, state, federal or foreign law.
-- A restriction for none of those purposes is not said to be unreasonable: NOTHING.
-- src:626 | Any restriction on the transfer or the registration of transfer of the securities of a corporation, or on the amount of securities of a corporation that may be owned by a person or group of persons, for any of the following purposes shall be conclusively presumed to be for a reasonable purpose:
-- src:627 | (1) Maintaining any local, state, federal or foreign tax advantage to the corporation or its stockholders, including without limitation:
-- src:628 | a. Maintaining the corporation’s status as an electing small business corporation under subchapter S of the United States Internal Revenue Code [26 U.S.C. § 1371 et seq.], or
-- src:629 | b. Maintaining or preserving any tax attribute (including without limitation net operating losses), or
-- src:630 | c. Qualifying or maintaining the qualification of the corporation as a real estate investment trust pursuant to the United States Internal Revenue Code or regulations adopted pursuant to the United States Internal Revenue Code, or
-- src:631 | (2) Maintaining any statutory or regulatory advantage or complying with any statutory or regulatory requirements under applicable local, state, federal or foreign law.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 202(d) (src:626-631)
DECLARE `s 202(d) The purpose of a restriction` HAS
    `maintaining a local, state, federal or foreign tax advantage to the corporation or its stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN
    `maintaining the corporation's status as an electing small business corporation under subchapter S of the United States Internal Revenue Code` IS A BOOLEAN
    `maintaining or preserving a tax attribute, including net operating losses` IS A BOOLEAN
    `qualifying or maintaining the qualification of the corporation as a real estate investment trust under the United States Internal Revenue Code` IS A BOOLEAN
    `maintaining a statutory or regulatory advantage or complying with a statutory or regulatory requirement under applicable local, state, federal or foreign law` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 202(d) (src:626-631)
GIVEN p IS A `s 202(d) The purpose of a restriction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202(d) the restriction is conclusively presumed to be for a reasonable purpose` p MEANS
    IF     p's `maintaining a local, state, federal or foreign tax advantage to the corporation or its stockholders`
       OR  p's `maintaining the corporation's status as an electing small business corporation under subchapter S of the United States Internal Revenue Code`
       OR  p's `maintaining or preserving a tax attribute, including net operating losses`
       OR  p's `qualifying or maintaining the qualification of the corporation as a real estate investment trust under the United States Internal Revenue Code`
       OR  p's `maintaining a statutory or regulatory advantage or complying with a statutory or regulatory requirement under applicable local, state, federal or foreign law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 202(e): any other lawful restriction on transfer or registration of transfer of securities, or on the amount that may be owned by any person or group, is permitted by the section.
-- A restriction is therefore permitted if it is of a kind in (c) or is another lawful restriction (whether it is lawful is a judgment: an input).
-- src:632 | Any other lawful restriction on transfer or registration of transfer of securities, or on the amount of securities that may be owned by any person or group of persons, is permitted by this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 202(e) (src:632)
GIVEN `the restriction is of a kind that section 202(c) permits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the restriction is otherwise lawful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 202(e) the restriction is permitted by section 202` `the restriction is of a kind that section 202(c) permits` `the restriction is otherwise lawful` MEANS
        `the restriction is of a kind that section 202(c) permits`
    OR  `the restriction is otherwise lawful`
